+### SDM630 energy meter (`ENABLE_SDM_METER`)
+
+Boards with an Eastron SDM630 / SDM72D-M (or compatible) meter on RS485 can read it over
+Modbus RTU. Build flags: `ENABLE_SDM_METER`, `SDM_METER_SERIAL` (default `Serial2`),
+`SDM_METER_RX`, `SDM_METER_TX`, `SDM_METER_BAUD` (9600), `SDM_METER_ADDRESS` (1). The RS485
+transceiver must switch direction by itself. When the meter answers, `/status` reports its
+values: `amp`/`voltage` (L1), `power` (total), `amp2`, `amp3`, `voltage2`, `voltage3`,
+`phases` (phases above 1 A), `meter_import_kwh`, `meter_valid`, `meter_present`, `meter_errors`, and the session
+energy is integrated from the measured total power. If the meter does not answer for 30 s
+(box sold without meter), `meter_present` turns `false`, the controller values are used and the
+meter is only probed once a minute. `DEBUG_PORT_NULL` sends debug output only to
+the web console, for boards where UART0 is the RAPI link.
